I can see the exact cause now — the visibility approach combined with the page structure is fighting you. The real culprit is that #field-techniques is a direct child of .container, and both the .container and the section are still taking up their full layout height in print, which creates those trailing blank pages. The heading leakage comes from the h2 and the first h3 inside the section still being visible because my selector logic was over-clever.

Let me give you a completely bulletproof approach that uses a known-tested pattern: instead of trying to hide everything and reveal pieces, we wrap the checklist in its own print-only container and use display: none on everything else. This is the pattern used by every reliable "print this section only" solution.

Step 1 — Add a wrapper around the checklist

In your #field-techniques section, wrap the checklist heading, list, and print button together in a single container. Change this:

```html
<h3 class="checklist-heading">Field Kit Checklist</h3>
<div class="checklist" id="fieldChecklist">
  ...items...
</div>
<button class="print-btn" onclick="window.print()">
  <i class="fas fa-print"></i> Print Checklist
</button>
```

To this:

```html
<div class="print-area" id="checklistArea">
  <h3 class="checklist-heading">Field Kit Checklist</h3>
  <div class="checklist" id="fieldChecklist">
    ...items... (unchanged)
  </div>
  <button class="print-btn" onclick="window.print()">
    <i class="fas fa-print"></i> Print Checklist
  </button>
</div>
```

Everything inside .print-area stays exactly as it is — just wrapped.

Step 2 — Replace the entire @media print block

Delete everything from /* ---------- PRINT: CHECKLIST ONLY ---------- */ down to the final } of that media block (including the stray brace and the orphaned section { page-break-inside: auto; } rules), and replace it with:

```css
/* ---------- PRINT: CHECKLIST ONLY ---------- */
@media print {
  /* Reset page */
  html, body {
    margin: 0 !important;
    padding: 0 !important;
    background: #fff !important;
    height: auto !important;
  }

  /* Hide the entire document by default */
  body > * {
    display: none !important;
  }

  /* Reveal ONLY the .container and everything up to the checklist area */
  body > .container {
    display: block !important;
    max-width: none !important;
    padding: 0 !important;
    margin: 0 !important;
  }

  /* Hide all sections except field-techniques */
  .container > section {
    display: none !important;
  }

  .container > #field-techniques {
    display: block !important;
    padding: 0 !important;
    margin: 0 !important;
    border: none !important;
    box-shadow: none !important;
    background: #fff !important;
  }

  /* Inside field-techniques, hide everything except the checklist area */
  #field-techniques > * {
    display: none !important;
  }

  #field-techniques > .print-area {
    display: block !important;
  }

  /* The print area itself */
  .print-area {
    display: block !important;
  }

  /* Title printed above the checklist */
  .print-area .checklist-heading {
    display: block !important;
    font-size: 1.4rem !important;
    font-weight: 700 !important;
    color: #1e3a1e !important;
    border-bottom: 3px solid #e6b422 !important;
    padding-bottom: 0.4rem !important;
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem !important;
  }

  /* The checklist layout for print */
  .print-area .checklist {
    display: block !important;
    width: 100% !important;
    margin: 0 !important;
    padding: 0 !important;
    grid-template-columns: none !important;
    gap: 0 !important;
  }

  .print-area .checklist-item {
    display: flex !important;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    padding: 0.4rem 0;
    background: none !important;
    border-bottom: 1px dotted #bbb;
    page-break-inside: avoid;
  }

  .print-area .checklist-item input[type="checkbox"] {
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
    accent-color: #000;
  }

  .print-area .checklist-item label {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: #000;
  }

  /* Hide the print button itself */
  .print-area .print-btn {
    display: none !important;
  }

  /* Optional: a small footer under the checklist */
  .print-area::after {
    content: "CIII CEM · Tasmanian Ecosystem Maintenance";
    display: block;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: #888;
    text-align: center;
  }
}
```

Why this works (and the previous attempts didn't)

The three previous failures each had a different root cause:

1. First version (visibility: hidden) — hidden elements still reserve layout height, so 8 pages of "invisible but present" content got printed as blank pages.
2. *Second version (display: none on body > ) — the sticky .nav-wrapper created a positioned context that forced the page to still be laid out, and the specificity of my nth-of-type heading selector was fragile.
3. Third version — same sticky problem, plus an imbalance of braces was silently breaking the stylesheet parsing.

The new approach is the standard pattern used by print-stylesheet libraries:

· body > * { display: none } removes everything from the layout tree — no reserved space, no blank pages.
· Then we walk back down the specific chain we need: .container → #field-techniques → .print-area → .checklist.
· Every other sibling gets re-hidden explicitly at each level (#field-techniques > * hides all direct children, then .print-area is re-revealed), so nothing leaks through.
· display: none truly removes elements from the render tree, so there is no layout contribution from hidden content — which is what eliminates the trailing blank pages.

Testing checklist

After you make the two changes above:

1. Open the file in your browser
2. Press Ctrl+P (or Cmd+P on Mac)
3. Check the preview — it should be 1 page (maybe 2 if the list is long on your paper size), starting with "Field Kit Checklist — CIII CEM" and ending with the small footer line
4. If your browser shows a different result, tell me which browser and OS — but this pattern is genuinely the most reliable one available
